{
  "id": "daily-temperatures",
  "questionId": "daily-temperatures",
  "slug": "daily-temperatures",
  "title": "Daily Temperatures",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Monotonic stack",
  "patterns": [
    "monotonic stack",
    "array"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "instead of each day searching forward on its own, what if colder days just 'waited' until a warmer day showed up and told them the answer directly?",
    "keep a stack of indices for days whose warmer day hasn't been found yet - what should happen to the indices on the stack the moment you see a temperature warmer than all of them?",
    "walk through the temperatures once; while the stack is non-empty and today's temperature is warmer than the temperature at the index on top of the stack, pop it and record today's index minus that popped index as its answer",
    "after resolving everything you can with today's temperature, push today's own index onto the stack, since it's now waiting for its own warmer day"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "storing temperatures on the stack instead of indices, making it impossible to compute the day difference",
    "using >= instead of > when comparing, which would treat an equal temperature as 'warmer'",
    "leaving indices on the stack unresolved at the end without their answer defaulting to 0"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of daily `temperatures`.\n\n**For each day, determine how many days you'd have to wait until a warmer temperature occurs, and return the results as an array, one value per day.**\n\nIf there's no future day with a warmer temperature, use 0 for that day instead.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "temperatures.length >= 1",
      "answer must count actual days waited, not the temperature difference"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "strictly decreasing temperatures, where every answer is 0",
      "a single day of temperatures",
      "repeated equal temperatures, which do not count as 'warmer'"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "temperatures = [73, 74, 75, 71, 69, 72, 76, 73]",
        "output": "[1, 1, 4, 2, 1, 1, 0, 0]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 1, 4, 2, 1, 1, 0, 0]",
        "explanation": "day 0 (73) waits 1 day for 74; day 2 (75) waits 4 days for 76; the last two days never see a warmer temperature"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "temperatures = [30, 40, 50, 60]",
        "output": "[1, 1, 1, 0]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 1, 1, 0]",
        "explanation": "each day is immediately followed by a warmer one, except the last"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
